From 9573f1315312ea4a49b39801ea297886258edcdf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 17:48:24 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Device names: one rule for Name and Hostname on every page

- Name is the name the admin gave on the Devices page, the one master list. Hostname is what the
  device sent, else the maker of its network card from a real MAC address, else Private-Address
  for a randomized one. A page with one label shows Name, else Hostname. A DHCP reservation's name
  is the device's DNS name and is labelled so.
- DHCP Leases: Name and Hostname columns, devices active with an address set on the device listed,
  Refresh shows it was pressed. Encrypted DNS, the dashboard, Devices, IPv6, LAN reservations,
  Wake-on-LAN, Parental Controls and Gatekeeper follow the rule; the maker is never looked up for
  a randomized MAC. Display only: every rule still keys on the MAC or address.
- Diagnostics: the Names, DNS names and announced names join its redaction list. Texts in all 25
  language packs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
